/E (The dataset was divided into training and testing sets using the train_test_split\(\) function from the sklearn.model_selection module to prepare the data for machine learning model development and evaluation. The review column was selected as the independent feature variable X, while the encoded sentiment labels stored in y were used as the target variable. The dataset was split with a test size of 20%, meaning that 80% of the data was used for training the machine learning models and 20% was reserved for testing and performance evaluation. The random_state=42 parameter was used to ensure reproducibility and consistency in the data splitting process. This step was important to evaluate how well the trained models could predict sentiments on unseen movie reviews and to measure their overall accuracy, reliability, and generalization performance.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
